From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Griffin <christophergriffin05@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 16:00:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] netifd: packet steering: spread wireless RSS flows over every
 CPU

B172. A wireless device with receive-side scaling (ath11k: one receive
ring and interrupt per CPU) was left without receive packet steering,
on the grounds that its rings already spread the load. But each ring
carries whole flows, so the driver, mac80211 and forwarding work of a
flow all run on one CPU, and the device can hash every flow of a
station onto one ring.

Arista C-360 (IPQ8074, QCN9074 6 GHz 160 MHz), one 2x2 HE station
uploading four TCP flows:

- all four flows on one ring: 1,015 Mbit/s with that ring's CPU at 98%
  softirq and the others at 20 to 30%;
- flows on three rings, steering switched on in mid-run (same flows):
  1,482 to 1,727 Mbit/s (+17%), hottest CPU 81% to 73%, no backlog
  drops. With steering on from the start: 1,641 Mbit/s.

Download is unchanged by it (1,584 to 1,566 in mid-run, noise), since
only ACKs arrive over the radio. Steering the ethernet side as well
gained nothing (+1 to +3.5%) and dropped packets at the backlog, so
ethernet devices with a queue per CPU stay as they are.

Give such a wireless device every CPU as its steering mask. And apply
steering when a wireless interface is made after boot: the service is
only reloaded on netifd interface events, which a radio restart does
not raise, so new interfaces stayed unsteered until the next one.

Bump PKG_RELEASE.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-fable-5-2
Signed-off-by: Christopher Griffin <christophergriffin05@gmail.com>
---
 package/network/config/netifd/Makefile          |  2 +-
 .../files/etc/hotplug.d/net/20-packet-steering  | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 .../usr/libexec/network/packet-steering.uc      |  7 +++++++
 3 files changed, 25 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/package/network/config/netifd/Makefile b/package/network/config/netifd/Makefile
index 42b6812ab59e34b6ccbe6e38640ec52ebf8afe24..40c1ffafce447d678fc3ff4aad509ee397364a28 100644
--- a/package/network/config/netifd/Makefile
+++ b/package/network/config/netifd/Makefile
@@ -1,7 +1,7 @@
 include $(TOPDIR)/rules.mk
 
 PKG_NAME:=netifd
-PKG_RELEASE:=4
+PKG_RELEASE:=5
 
 PKG_SOURCE_PROTO:=git
 PKG_SOURCE_URL=$(PROJECT_GIT)/project/netifd.git
diff --git a/package/network/config/netifd/files/etc/hotplug.d/net/20-packet-steering b/package/network/config/netifd/files/etc/hotplug.d/net/20-packet-steering
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..32f391381be2c7ce13aaccc817ff9faa34a40965
--- /dev/null
+++ b/package/network/config/netifd/files/etc/hotplug.d/net/20-packet-steering
@@ -0,0 +1,17 @@
+#!/bin/sh
+# A wireless interface made after boot has no receive packet steering until
+# the next interface event: apply it now. One run covers the interfaces a
+# radio brings up together.
+
+[ "$ACTION" = add ] && [ "$DEVTYPE" = wlan ] || exit 0
+[ -x /etc/init.d/packet_steering ] || exit 0
+
+PENDING=/var/run/packet-steering.pending
+[ -e "$PENDING" ] && exit 0
+touch "$PENDING"
+
+(
+	sleep 3
+	rm -f "$PENDING"
+	/etc/init.d/packet_steering reload
+) &
diff --git a/package/network/config/netifd/files/usr/libexec/network/packet-steering.uc b/package/network/config/netifd/files/usr/libexec/network/packet-steering.uc
index 853845ecaa2b793e38f956bb71366544bf948e14..32d9d3d24c0731fea42fc209f84e062850f800c7 100755
--- a/package/network/config/netifd/files/usr/libexec/network/packet-steering.uc
+++ b/package/network/config/netifd/files/usr/libexec/network/packet-steering.uc
@@ -357,6 +357,13 @@ function assign_dev_cpu(dev) {
 			cpu = -1;
 		else if (rps_cpus)
 			cpu = rps_cpus;
+		else if (hw_spread && dev.rss)
+			// A receive ring of a wireless device carries whole
+			// flows, and the driver, mac80211 and forwarding work of
+			// a flow all run on that ring's CPU. The device can also
+			// hash every flow of a station onto one ring. Let the
+			// stack half of the work go to any CPU.
+			cpu = -1;
 		else if (!hw_spread)
 			cpu = get_next_cpu(rx_weight, dev.napi_cpu);
 		for (let netdev in dev.netdev)
-- 
2.43.0

